#: functions/bang_bang_on_off.py:17
msgid "Bang-Bang Hysteretic (On/Off) (Raise/Lower/Both)"
msgstr ""

#: functions/bang_bang_on_off.py:20
msgid ""
"A simple Bang-Bang control method that uses a single input value to control "
"one or two outputs. Select the input, configure the Raise and/or Lower "
"outputs, then enter the **Setpoint and Hysteresis (operating range) and "
"choose the Direction.     •\tRaise mode (e.g., heating): the output turns on"
" when the input is at or below (setpoint - hysteresis), and turns off when "
"the input is at or above (setpoint + hysteresis).     •\tLower mode (e.g., "
"cooling): the opposite of the above, turning the output on to lower the "
"input.     •\tBoth: adjusts Raise and Lower to keep the input at the "
"setpoint."
msgstr ""

#: functions/bang_bang_pwm.py:16
msgid "Bang-Bang Hysteretic (PWM) (Raise/Lower/Both)"
msgstr ""

#: functions/bang_bang_pwm.py:19
msgid ""
"A simple Bang-Bang control method that uses a single input value to control "
"one PWM output. Select the input, enter the PWM output, Setpoint, and "
"**Hysteresis**, then choose the Direction. \t•\tRaise mode (e.g., heating): "
"the output turns on when the input is at or below (setpoint - hysteresis), "
"and turns off when the input is at or above (setpoint + hysteresis). "
"\t•\tLower mode (e.g., cooling): the opposite of the above, turning the "
"output on to lower the input. \t•\tBoth mode: adjusts Raise and Lower to "
"keep the input at the setpoint. Note: this output only works with a PWM "
"(Pulse Width Modulation) output."
msgstr ""

