"then channels 2 and 3, then channels 4 and 5, and so on. After all channels "
"have been displayed, it cycles back to the beginning."
msgstr ""

#: functions/display_ssd1306_oled_128x32_i2c.py:171
msgid ""
"This function provides output to a 128x32 SSD1306 OLED display over I2C. "
"This display function can show 4 lines at a time, so each change to the "
"Number of Line Sets adds 4 channels. The LCD refreshes every configured "
"Period, displaying the next set of lines. So the first displayed line set is"
" channels 0 - 3, then 4 - 7, then 8 - 11, and so on. After all channels have"
" been displayed, it cycles back to the beginning."
msgstr ""

